### Component 1: Dataset Preparation (`training/dataset.py`)

#### [NEW] [dataset.py](file:///c:/Users/Shloka%20Pol/OneDrive/Desktop/fin_modal1/training/dataset.py)

- **Unified Dataset class** — merges `output/dataset.csv` and `output_pan/pan_dataset.csv` into one training set
- **Train/Val/Test split** — 70/15/15 stratified by label AND doc type
- **Spatial transforms** — resize to 300×300, random horizontal flip, color jitter, random erasing, normalize (ImageNet stats)
- **Frequency transforms** — compute 2D DCT coefficients per channel, log-scale, resize to 300×300
- **Test-time** — deterministic center-crop + resize only

---

### Component 2: DCT Utilities (`training/dct_utils.py`)

#### [NEW] [dct_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/Shloka%20Pol/OneDrive/Desktop/fin_modal1/training/dct_utils.py)

- `compute_dct(image_tensor)` → applies `scipy.fft.dctn` per channel
- `log_scale_dct(dct_coefficients)` → `log(1 + |coefficients|)` to compress dynamic range
- GAN-generated images show distinctive high-frequency energy patterns that this captures

---

### Component 3: Dual-Branch Model (`training/model.py`)

#### [NEW] [model.py](file:///c:/Users/Shloka%20Pol/OneDrive/Desktop/fin_modal1/training/model.py)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              DUAL-BRANCH FORGERY DETECTOR                │
├──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┤
│   SPATIAL BRANCH     │    FREQUENCY BRANCH              │
│                      │                                  │
│  Input: RGB 300×300  │  Input: DCT 300×300 (3-ch)       │
│         ↓            │         ↓                        │
│  EfficientNet-B3     │  Conv(3→32, 3×3) + BN + ReLU    │
│  (ImageNet weights)  │  Conv(32→64, 3×3) + BN + ReLU   │
│  freeze first 4      │  MaxPool(2×2)                    │
│  blocks initially    │  Conv(64→128, 3×3) + BN + ReLU  │
│         ↓            │  GlobalAvgPool                   │
│  AdaptiveAvgPool     │         ↓                        │
│         ↓            │  FC(128 → 256)                   │
│  1280-dim features   │  256-dim features                │
├──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┤
│                    FUSION HEAD                           │
│                                                         │
│  Concat(1280 + 256) = 1536-dim                          │
│         ↓                                               │
│  FC(1536 → 512) + BN + ReLU + Dropout(0.4)             │
│  FC(512 → 128) + BN + ReLU + Dropout(0.3)              │
│  FC(128 → 2)                                            │
│         ↓                                               │
│  Softmax → [P(real), P(fake)]                           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- **Loss**: Focal Loss (γ=2, α=0.25) to handle class imbalance
- **Optimizer**: AdamW (lr=1e-4 spatial, lr=5e-4 frequency, lr=1e-3 fusion)
- **Scheduler**: CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts
- **Framework**: PyTorch + timm (for EfficientNet-B3)

---

### Component 4: Training Loop (`training/train.py`)

#### [NEW] [train.py](file:///c:/Users/Shloka%20Pol/OneDrive/Desktop/fin_modal1/training/train.py)

**Phase 1: Warm-up (5 epochs)**
- Freeze EfficientNet-B3 backbone (first 4 blocks)
- Train only frequency branch + fusion head
- LR = 1e-3

**Phase 2: Fine-tuning (25–40 epochs)**
- Unfreeze all layers
- Differential LR: backbone=1e-5, frequency=5e-4, fusion=1e-3
- Early stopping (patience=7) on validation loss

**Features:**
- Mixed-precision training (FP16) if GPU available
- TensorBoard logging (loss, accuracy, LR curves)
- Best model checkpoint saving
- Gradient clipping (max_norm=1.0)

