### Component 6: Semantic Consistency Validator (`training/semantic_validator.py`)

#### [NEW] [semantic_validator.py](file:///c:/Users/Shloka%20Pol/OneDrive/Desktop/fin_modal1/training/semantic_validator.py)

This is a **rule-based module** (no ML training needed) with three sub-components:

**A. Text Extraction (EasyOCR)**
```python
# Extract fields from document image
{
    "name": "RAJESH KUMAR",
    "dob": "15/08/1990",
    "gender": "Male",
    "id_number": "1234 5678 9012",  # Aadhaar
    "pan_number": "ABCPK1234F",     # PAN
    "father_name": "SURESH KUMAR",  # PAN only
    "doc_type": "aadhaar" | "pan"
}
```

**B. Rule-Based Validation**
| Check | Rule | Fail = Suspicious |
|-------|------|-------------------|
| Aadhaar format | `\d{4}\s\d{4}\s\d{4}`, Verhoeff checksum | ✗ |
| PAN format | `[A-Z]{3}[ABCFGHLJPT][A-Z]\d{4}[A-Z]` | ✗ |
| DOB validity | Valid date, age 18–100, not future | ✗ |
| Name characters | Only `[A-Za-z\s.]`, length 3–50 | ✗ |
| Gender values | Must be "Male" / "Female" / "Transgender" | ✗ |

**C. Semantic Cross-Validation**
| Check | Method |
|-------|--------|
| Name ↔ Gender consistency | Name-gender lookup (Indian name DB) |
| DOB ↔ Face age consistency | DeepFace age estimation vs DOB age (±10yr tolerance) |
| Father's name ≠ Applicant name | String comparison |
| PAN 5th char = surname initial | Check PAN[4] matches name surname[0] |

**Output: Semantic risk score (0.0 – 1.0)**

